101	-        run: zig fmt --check zig-parquet/src zig-parquet/build.zig zig-parquet/bench cli/src cli/build.zig
102	+        run: zig fmt --check zig-parquet/src zig-parquet/build.zig zig-parquet/bench zig-parquet/fuzz cli/src cli/build.zig
103	 
104	   interop:
105	     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
106	diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
107	index 5bf0f2d..5c9022e 100644
108	--- a/CHANGELOG.md
109	+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
110	@@ -4,6 +4,9 @@ All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
111	 
112	 ## [Unreleased]
113	 
114	+### Data corruption fix: GZIP pages
115	+- **The pure-Zig gzip encoder wrote invalid deflate streams for ordinary data** (since v0.1.6, including v0.2.0). Its Huffman tree builder clamped codes deeper than the length limit, producing an oversubscribed prefix code, so neither zig-parquet nor zlib could read the page back. In tests, 33 of 128 realistic page payloads (timestamps, skewed bytes, text, 8 KiB to 1 MiB) were affected. **GZIP-compressed files written by zig-parquet v0.1.6 to v0.2.0 may contain unreadable pages; rewrite them with this version.** Files written with other codecs, or with the C gzip codec (`c-gzip`), are not affected.
116	+
117	 ### Performance
118	 - Streaming row iterator: `DynamicReader.rowIteratorStreaming()` and `rowIteratorStreamingProjected()` return a `StreamingRowIterator` that reuses one row buffer. Contract: the row and its byte slices are valid until the next `next()` or `deinit()`. Memory is bounded by one row group. If loading a row group fails, the next `next()` retries that row group.
119	 - Zero-copy byte arrays on flat reads: PLAIN and dictionary BYTE_ARRAY values (V1 and V2) are slices of the page buffer instead of per-value copies.
120	@@ -27,6 +30,7 @@ Benchmark, ReleaseFast, zig-only codecs, 1,000,000 rows, Zig 0.16.0, Ryzen 9 795
121	 Output bytes are unchanged: file sizes match the baseline in every scenario, and golden-byte tests cover the changed write paths.
122	 
123	 ### Added
124	+- Fuzz harness (`zig-parquet/fuzz/`): six targets (file, file-oom, page, encoding, thrift, codec) with a mutation loop that runs on every OS, Zig's coverage-guided fuzzer on Linux/macOS, corpus replay in `zig build test`, a minimizer and a regression convention. `make fuzz-run`, `make fuzz-replay`, `make fuzz-cov`. A manual-only GitHub workflow (`fuzz.yml`) runs it in CI on demand.
125	 - `Row.values_borrowed` flag (default `false`) for rows whose value block is owned by the producer.
126	 - `StreamingRowIterator` is exported from the package root.
127	 - `make bench` target (zig-only, ReleaseFast; `ROWS=<n>` sets the row count).
128	@@ -40,6 +44,14 @@ Output bytes are unchanged: file sizes match the baseline in every scenario, and
129	 - C codec dependencies are lazy: zig-only builds no longer fetch the C codec archives.
130	 
131	 ### Fixed
132	+- DELTA_BINARY_PACKED: deltas now wrap at the column's type width as the spec requires. INT32 columns with consecutive values more than 2^31 apart were written with a delta the reader rejected, and INT64 extremes panicked the encoder. The decoder also decoded zigzag values of 2^62 or more as -1, and misread 58- to 63-bit-wide values at unaligned offsets.
133	+- Brotli decompression read code-length bits past the end of truncated input (integer overflow); malformed prefix codes are now rejected as in RFC 7932.
134	+- Gzip decompression panicked on some truncated streams under Zig 0.16 (a sign error in std 0.16's inflate, fixed in 0.17); it now returns `error.DecompressionError` on both versions.
135	+- Leaks on malformed footers: repeated `ColumnIndex`/`OffsetIndex` fields and partially parsed page headers are freed.
136	+- `DynamicReader.deinit`, and the C and WASM reader handles, leaked schema logical-type payloads such as a GEOGRAPHY `crs`. They now free the whole footer.
137	+- Leaks when a page fails to decode part-way: def/rep levels and byte values already copied are freed. Also fixed a leak when an allocation fails while a nested column result is assembled.
138	+- Untrusted counts could ask for huge allocations: a page claiming more values than its column chunk, a column chunk past the end of the file, a row group whose `num_rows` exceeds the values actually decoded, and a dictionary with more entries than its page can hold. Each now returns an error before allocating.
139	+- List and map columns with fewer repetition levels than definition levels panicked; they now return `error.InvalidRepetitionLevels`.
140	 - Bit unpacking overflowed `u5` for bit widths 25-31: the byte count was computed in `u5`. This panicked in Debug builds and gave a wrong byte count in ReleaseFast. Fixed by computing in `usize`.
141	 - Overflow-checked level and bit-pack sizes: `bitPackedSize` returns `error.Overflow`, and V2 level cursor checks are overflow-safe.
142	 - Out-of-memory leaks: footer parsers (`ColumnChunk`, `Statistics`, `RowGroup`, `SchemaElement`, `KeyValue`, `FileMetaData`) free partial allocations; nested assembly frees the partial list item and struct field; dynamic decoders free def/rep levels and page results.
